Question 18: Do you have other comments or suggestions for Cheyenne’s parks, trails, and open spaces
system?

Respondents were asked to provide any additional comments or suggestions that they had for the future of
Cheyenne’s Parks and Recreation System. The question received 201 responses, listed in the Open-ended Question
Responses. The responses were organized into the following larger themes.

Improved Connectivity and Safety of Greenway and Trails:
•
Better connect the Greenway through the heart of the city to make it safer and more usable.
•
Address safety concerns at crossings and intersections.
•
Ensure the Greenway connects more comprehensively throughout the city and downtown areas.
Development of Indoor Recreational Facilities:
•
Build additional indoor recreation centers, including spaces for various sports like tennis, pickleball,
basketball, and ice hockey.
•
Emphasize year-round accessibility to indoor facilities due to harsh weather conditions.
•
Provide affordable indoor options for swimming and other activities.
Enhancement of Existing Parks and Facilities:
•
Add amenities such as benches, trash cans, bathrooms, and interpretation trails.
•
Maintain and improve current facilities rather than expanding new ones.
•
Address cleanliness, safety, and maintenance issues, including managing the homeless population
in parks.
•
Enhancements to existing parks, including more shade structures, flowering trees, and improved
accessibility.
•
Expansion and better maintenance of greenways and trails, with some advocating for new
connections and extensions.
•
Interest in developing new parks and open spaces, particularly in underserved areas of the city.
